[sanitizer_common] [Darwin] Adopt _dyld_get_dyld_header

Backport to compiler-rt 21.1.8 of upstream LLVM commit
2e7d07a33725a82ecfc514e27f047ece3ff13d4c
"[sanitizer_common] [Darwin] Adopt _dyld_get_dyld_header (#182943)"
by Andrew Haberlandt <ahaberlandt@apple.com>, 2026-02-24, cherry-picked to
release/22.x as 7b6514cd3089 (first released in llvmorg-22.1.3).

Only the _dyld_get_dyld_header change is carried: the weak declaration, the
early return from GetDyldImageHeaderViaSharedCache, its weak_symbols.txt
entry, and the const-correctness the early return needs (dyld_hdr and the
function's return type become `const mach_header *`). The surrounding
21.1.8 code differs from release/22.x in unrelated ways and is unchanged.

Why: on macOS 26, dyld_shared_cache_iterate_text copies its callback block
(_Block_copy -> malloc). Reached from InitializeShadowMemory -> get_dyld_hdr
during AsanInitInternal, that malloc re-enters AsanInitFromRtl, which spins
forever on the init mutex it already holds, so every ASan program hangs
before main. _dyld_get_dyld_header returns the header directly; the weak
import keeps older macOS on the shared-cache walk.

--- a/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_procmaps_mac.cpp
+++ b/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_procmaps_mac.cpp
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@
 // The dyld load address should be unchanged throughout process execution,
 // and it is expensive to compute once many libraries have been loaded,
 // so cache it here and do not reset.
-static mach_header *dyld_hdr = 0;
+static const mach_header *dyld_hdr = 0;
 static const char kDyldPath[] = "/usr/lib/dyld";
 static const int kDyldImageIdx = -1;
 
@@ -190,13 +190,17 @@
 extern int dyld_shared_cache_iterate_text(
     const uuid_t cacheUuid,
     void (^callback)(const dyld_shared_cache_dylib_text_info *info));
+SANITIZER_WEAK_IMPORT const struct mach_header *_dyld_get_dyld_header(void);
 }  // extern "C"
 
-static mach_header *GetDyldImageHeaderViaSharedCache() {
+static const mach_header *GetDyldImageHeaderViaSharedCache() {
   uuid_t uuid;
   bool hasCache = _dyld_get_shared_cache_uuid(uuid);
   if (!hasCache)
     return nullptr;
+
+  if (&_dyld_get_dyld_header != nullptr)
+    return _dyld_get_dyld_header();
 
   size_t cacheLength;
   __block uptr cacheStart = (uptr)_dyld_get_shared_cache_range(&cacheLength);
--- a/lib/sanitizer_common/weak_symbols.txt
+++ b/lib/sanitizer_common/weak_symbols.txt
@@ -10,3 +10,4 @@
 ___sanitizer_symbolize_flush
 ___sanitizer_symbolize_set_demangle
 ___sanitizer_symbolize_set_inline_frames
+__dyld_get_dyld_header
